drm: sunxi_drm_edp: adopt an already-connected sink at bind

The sink extcon notifier only delivers edges, so a sink that was already
connected before this driver existed is never announced.

That is the ordinary case when the cable is in at power-on. On a Cubie A7S the
Type-C stack finishes negotiating DP alt mode and the combo PHY publishes
EXTCON_DISP_DP well before drm_edp binds:

  [ 4.782] set mux state STATE_SAFE -> STATE_DP_D   status:0x1a
  [ 5.032] set mux state STATE_DP_D -> STATE_DP_D   status:0x9a   <- extcon DP=1
  [ 5.465] sunxi-drm: bound 5740000.edp0                          <- listener appears

The event lands with nobody subscribed. The provider extcon then reads DP=1
while the connector sits at "disconnected" indefinitely, and the only ways out
are a physical re-plug or a manual
"echo detect > /sys/class/drm/card0-DP-1/status". That manual step has been
mistaken for a detect race before; it is really this missed edge.

Read the level once, after subscribing to the edges. Ordering matters: register
first, so a change racing the read is either caught by the notifier or visible
in what is read, and cannot be missed by both.

Only the flag is set here. The detect kthread has not started at this point, so
it observes hpd_state_now != hpd_state on its first pass and runs the ordinary
plug path once the hardware is up, instead of driving AUX from probe context.

Signed-off-by: Paul Goldsmith <goldfish.paul@gmail.com>
---
--- a/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_edp.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_edp.c
@@ -3036,6 +3036,33 @@
 			DRM_ERROR("register extcon notifier for edp fail\n");
 			goto ERR_CLK;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * The notifier only delivers edges, so a sink that was already
+		 * connected before this driver existed is never announced.
+		 *
+		 * That is the normal case when the cable is in at power-on: on
+		 * the Cubie A7S, Type-C finishes negotiating DP alt mode and the
+		 * combo PHY publishes EXTCON_DISP_DP at about t=5.03s, while
+		 * drm_edp does not bind until t=5.47s. The event lands with no
+		 * listener, the connector stays "disconnected" forever, and the
+		 * only way out is a physical re-plug or a manual
+		 * "echo detect > /sys/class/drm/card0-DP-1/status".
+		 *
+		 * Take the level after subscribing to the edges. Ordering
+		 * matters: registering first means a change racing this read is
+		 * either caught by the notifier or reflected in what we read,
+		 * never dropped by both.
+		 *
+		 * Only the flag is set here. The detect kthread has not started
+		 * yet, so it picks this up as a hpd_state_now != hpd_state edge
+		 * on its first pass and runs the normal plug path once the
+		 * hardware is actually up - rather than doing AUX from probe.
+		 */
+		if (extcon_get_state(drm_edp->extcon_sink, EXTCON_DISP_DP) > 0) {
+			EDP_DRV_DBG("sink already connected at bind, seeding hpd\n");
+			drm_edp->hpd_state_now = true;
+		}
 	}
 #endif
 
